---
/*
  ComingUpZone — what is approaching, on its own terms
  (docs/plans/13-agenda.md §6; 10-hq.md §10c).

  ⚠ DRIVEN ENTIRELY BY EACH ITEM'S OWN LEAD, and "entirely" is the plan's own
  emphasis. A `project` announces itself 21 days out; a `quick` task the day
  before; a birthday at whatever `birthday_lead_days` says. There is no "next 7
  days" setting anywhere in this feature, and its absence is the point: **the
  list is short because the leads are honest.** When it gets long the fix is the
  effort on a task, not a dial on a page.

  Which is also why it is UNCAPPED, unlike past due. A cap would be the window
  arriving again under another name.

  ⚠ BIRTHDAYS LIVE HERE NOW, not in People (settled 2026-08-03). 12 · Piece 4 put
  them in the People zone and said so in a comment — because a "Coming up" zone
  whose only possible content was birthdays would have misrepresented a zone that
  was about to mean something else. It means something else now. A birthday needs
  runway for exactly the reason a task does: you have to find time to do
  something about it.

  The cost is real and was weighed: a person's name now sits in an amber agenda
  zone rather than the azure people one, so the domain hue no longer says what it
  is. The cake carries that instead — one glyph, in place, rather than a second
  zone repeating a name that is already on the page (§10i).

  A BIRTHDAY *TODAY* IS NOT HERE — it is on the day itself, with the day's other
  things. Coming up means not yet.

  `o-4`: on a phone People comes before this, because who you are seeing today
  matters more than what is approaching (§10b).
*/
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import Zone from './Zone.astro';
import type { CalendarItem } from '../../lib/hq/calendar';
import { clockTime, dmd, fullDate } from '../../lib/hq/dates';
import { byDayThenTime } from '../../lib/hq/today';
import type { Ymd } from '../../lib/hq/time';

interface Props {
  items: CalendarItem[];
  today: Ymd;
}
const { items, today } = Astro.props;
const rows = [...items].sort(byDayThenTime);
---

{
  rows.length > 0 && (
    <Zone title="Coming up" icon="ph:clock-light" accent="cn-amber" order={4} data-coming-up>
      <a slot="actions" class="zone__act" href="/admin/agenda/tasks" aria-label="Open tasks">
        <Icon name="ph:arrow-right" />
      </a>

      <div class="zone__body">
        {rows.map((it) => (
          <div class="row" data-id={it.id} data-kind={it.kind}>
            {/* No tick. Nothing here is due yet, and offering to complete
                something ahead of its lead is how a lead becomes a deadline. */}
            <span class="row__time row__time--wide" title={fullDate(it.on)}>
              {dmd(it.on, today)}
            </span>
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              {it.href ? (
                <a class="row__t row-open" href={it.href}>
                  {it.kind === 'birthday' && <Icon name="ph:cake" class="row__i" />}
                  {it.title}
                </a>
              ) : (
                <span class="row__t">{it.title}</span>
              )}
              {it.at && <span class="row__sub">{clockTime(it.at)}</span>}
            </span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </Zone>
  )
}
